laying the lower ♥5 gives my teammate (who holds 2 cards) a better chance to win the trick with a mid-range card like 6, 7, or 8 — if they hold such a card, they can take control and possibly clear their hand before the landlord does.\n\nThus, **playing the lower card (♥5)** gives more space for my teammate to intervene, while preserving slightly better coordination.\n\nReason: As a peasant, my goal is to help my teammate block the landlord. By playing the smaller card (♥5), I minimize pressure and allow my teammate flexibility to play a slightly higher card (like 6 or 7) to win the trick — especially since they still hold 2 cards and may be trying to finish. The landlord is on their last card, so avoiding unnecessary aggression is key. Playing too high (♦7) risks forcing my teammate to pass if they don\'t have an 8 or above, handing control directly to the landlord.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♥5"]}'}
